From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shm_unlink: translate sticky-directory denial to EACCES

POSIX specifies EACCES when removal of a shared-memory object is denied.
Linux unlink can instead report EPERM for sticky-directory ownership checks.
Translate that error at the shm interface, as glibc does, while preserving
all other errors and the underlying unlink semantics.

diff --git a/librt/shm.c b/librt/shm.c
--- a/librt/shm.c
+++ b/librt/shm.c
@@ -102,6 +102,9 @@ int shm_unlink(const char *name)
 	if (shm_name == NULL)
 		return -1;
 	ret = unlink(shm_name);
+	/* POSIX requires EACCES for permission denied to shm_unlink. */
+	if (ret < 0 && errno == EPERM)
+		__set_errno(EACCES);
 	free(shm_name); /* doesn't affect errno */
 	return ret;
 }
